### Phase X — Operator Intelligence (2026-05-04)
Three-part upgrade so the owner/operator interface acts like an ops assistant rather than
a database tool. Every reply is fast, includes one operator-facing insight, and never
exposes DB internals or "no records" copy.

- (a) ownerMode.buildOwnerInstruction rewritten with the Phase X spec: two-layer
  awareness, context-inheritance rules, intent mapping (kremmling → location;
  REA / Rabbit Ears / CSR → company), empty-state hard rules (never "no records",
  never expose Supabase / CRM / tables), required one-line insight, Phase-X bullet
  template, seasonal business context (Summer=RZRs, Winter=snowmobiles, Kremmling
  primary). Null-fallback also hides DB references.
- (b) Operator context memory across turns. operatorIntentParser.js exports
  isVagueFollowUp / mergeOperatorContext / extractOperatorContext. FILLER_STARTS
  extended with and/or/but/& to fix spurious company_filter extraction on
  metric-only refinements. operatorBriefing.detectAndHandleOperatorCommand
  accepts an optional convo arg: reads prior context off booking_data._operator,
  merges it into the parsed intent, persists the new context after each
  successful structured route. Bare-revenue intercept defers to the structured
  path when inherited context provides a date_range. agentOrchestrator.js threads
  convo through. "kremmling" / "what about steamboat?" / "and revenue?" inherit
  timeframe + entity + metric from the prior turn.
- (c) Fallback intelligence + insight + Phase-X format (actionEngine.js).
  buildOperatorInsight (exported pure helper) picks one insight per response from
  a strategy ladder: location dominance → barely-contributing 2nd → company
  dominance → small-group pattern → top activity. formatPhaseXBookingReply
  renders {Scope} header, • Bookings / Guests / Revenue bullets, insight,
  optional By location: / By company: / Top activities:. handleGetBookingsByDateRange
  retry ladder on 0 rows: drop location → drop company → broaden to last 90 days,
  each level prepending "I'm not seeing X — here's Y:". Truly-empty state suggests
  a campaign instead of "no records". handleReport adopts the same bullet format
  + insight in result.insight. All "I couldn't find any records … adjust the
  timeframe or filters" copy removed.

Tests: +62 assertions in test.js — 2138/2138 passing. Covers the new ownerMode
rules, isVagueFollowUp / merge / extract, convo persistence + inheritance round-trip,
buildOperatorInsight branches, fallback retry, Phase-X format on bookings + report
handlers.

